@startuml mf-02a-reserve-aim
' SRS Section II.1.2.2 — Main Workflow: Delivery, part A (Reserve & Aim)
' Continues in mf-02b-commit-dropoff-retreat.puml
' Supersedes mf-02a-approach.puml: the approach leg was retired when the drop-off
' slot became dynamic — the vehicle is aimed at a slot of its own instead.
' Business-level vocabulary only; implementation detail belongs in the SDS.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng mf-02a-reserve-aim.puml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam swimlaneWidth 260
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999

title Delivery - Part A: Reserve & Aim

|#F2F2F2|FMS (openTCS)|
start
:The pick-up transport order\nreaches FINISHED;
:Notify WES;
note right
  WES re-checks the order state on a
  heartbeat, so a lost notification
  does not stall the task
end note

|#FFFFFF|WES|
:Receive the pick-up completion;
if (Drop-off order\nalready issued?) then (Yes)
  :Ignore the duplicate notification;
  stop
else (No)
endif
if (Assigned vehicle and\ndestination zone both present?) then (No)
  :Task -> FAILED;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
:Take exclusive access to\nthe zone's slot map;
note right
  Both slot steps run under exclusive
  access, so two vehicles arriving at
  once are never given the same slot
end note
:Reserve one concrete drop-off slot by the\ncascading depth-first fill rule (BR-11),\ncounting the slots already COMMITTED\nand the slots already RESERVED;
if (Any slot free\nto reserve?) then (No)
  :Release the zone;
  :Stay in PICKING_UP;\nthe periodic re-check retries;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
:Record the slot on the cargo\nas a PROVISIONAL RESERVATION;
:Release the zone;
note right
  A reservation is **provisional**: it only
  records the slot WES currently intends
  the cargo to occupy. Part B may still
  **swap** it away, and only the **commit**
  in Part B makes a slot binding.
end note
:Resolve the 2-cell retreat path\nbehind the reserved slot;
if (Retreat path found?) then (No)
  :Log a warning - the drop-off order\ngoes out without the retreat steps;
else (Yes)
endif
:Issue ONE drop-off transport order aimed at the\nreserved slot: unload at the slot, then one\nmove step per retreat cell;
:Task -> DELIVERING;
note right
  There is no approach order and no shared
  approach point. Each vehicle drives from
  the pick-up straight to a slot of its own,
  so two vehicles are never routed to the
  same destination.
end note

|#F2F2F2|FMS (openTCS)|
:Route the vehicle towards\nthe reserved slot;

|#F2F2F2|AGV|
:Drive towards the destination zone;
note right
  Continues in Part B:
  Commit, Swap, Drop-off & Retreat
end note
stop

@enduml
